      "content": "Introduction"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Huffman coding is an algorithm designed for data compression. This technique uses binary trees to reduce the size of data."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "It's the underlying mechanism in popular compression formats like GZIP and BZIP2."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Why is compression necessary?"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "When transmitting or storing large files, the absence of compression can lead to high costs and inefficiencies."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Suppose we have a string with some repeated characters."
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "alt": "String to Shrink Size Using Huffman Coding",
      "src": "data:image/png;base64,"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Each character in the string uses 8 bits."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "For 15 characters, that's 120 bits total which is a lot of space."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "As there are recurring characters in the string, we can reduce the size based on the frequency of each character. This can be accomplished using Huffman coding."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Next, we will implement Huffman coding to compress a string."
    },
